diff --git a/docs/assigned-task-isolation.md b/docs/assigned-task-isolation.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..49d3aa30
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/assigned-task-isolation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Assigned-task execution isolation
+
+The packaged daemon sets `act.Config.SerialJobs` for each assignment. Independent jobs and matrix entries expanded locally, including nested reusable workflows, share that assignment's serial execution policy. Separate assignments retain poller capacity. Library/exec callers leave this opt-in flag unset unless they request the same bound; no global semaphore spans reusable callers.
+
+Action downloads use a fresh private task directory, removed when execution returns. Shared Git clones and abandoned Git index locks are not reused or deleted. Remote metadata, generated fallback files and compatibility bundle edits use an opened repository root. Dockerfiles and build contexts must remain within that repository; `.dockerignore` must remain within its context. Local generated action files are copied through the container API instead of written to the controller.
+
+Docker labels may append `?platform=linux/arm64` or another Docker platform. The image reference excludes the query. Platform selection evaluates each expanded job's `runs-on`, applies to job/service/action containers and image builds, and survives reusable workflow configuration copies. Without a matching label platform, the existing runner-wide architecture remains the fallback. Installing binfmt alone does not select a platform.
+
+`RUNNER_ROOT_CA` optionally names an operator-owned public CA PEM bundle on the controller. Private keys, non-CA certificates, malformed PEM and extra data are rejected. The public certificate is copied into the job's system trust and shared action volume, and the supported system CA updater runs as user 0 before workflow actions. Node receives `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` for the shared public certificate. Custom Docker-action and service images still own their system trust stores.
+
+Runner-level Gitea client-certificate fields are not the Docker mTLS identity. Builtin checkout can copy those configured Gitea client keys into a job; a VM package must leave those fields unset. Docker client private keys and persistent registration remain controller-only.
